As JSON text — this is what crosses the network:
{
  "sku": "MRD-CLE-001",
  "qty": 480,
  "unit_price": 12.5,
  "in_stock": true,
  "discontinued_on": null,
  "tags": [
    "cleaning",
    "bulk"
  ],
  "supplier": {
    "name": "Voss Industrial",
    "tier": "Strategic"
  }
}

And back again:
  sku              str
  qty              int
  unit_price       float
  in_stock         bool
  discontinued_on  NoneType
  tags             list
  supplier         dict

Identical after the round trip? True

Dictionary with integer keys: {1: 'one', 2: 'two'}
After a JSON round trip:       {'1': 'one', '2': 'two'}
JSON object keys are always strings. Nothing else survives.
